  "problem": "Daniel bought $8$ cookies for $$4.$ What statement describes the unit rate?",
  "worked_solution": "The ratio of cookies to dollars is $8:4.$ So we start with the ratio $8:4$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $1$ by dividing the numerator and denominator by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8÷4}{4÷4}=\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nConsequently, Daniel bought $2$ cookies per dollar.",
